S3L = {
8: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Single (one data type)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital construction site layout planning and real-time trajectory analysis for proactive safety monitoring and control of struck-by hazards (DTCS Right-time Analysis and Mitigation module; DTU/TUM): RTK-GNSS + LoRa live location tracking of pedestrian workers and heavy equipment streamed to DTCS; semi-static and dynamic hazard zones (1-m boundary + operator blind-space geometry); real-time incident detection of unauthorized entry and too-close proximity; density maps / histogram heatmaps identify hazardous activities; safety-plan revision recommendations (separating worker/equipment areas, temporary pedestrian walkways); field experiments in Munich subway rail maintenance staging area showed significant reduction in spatial conflicts and improved zone connectivity, with newly detected hazards (rail traffic, delivery trucks) triggering iterative plan updates. One-way monitoring to analysis to mitigation recommendations/alerts for safety personnel; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
26: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 1, 1, 1, 'Both', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Full-cycle municipal pipeline DT platform (Shanghai Oriental Hub): BIM0–BIM6 full-phase connection + lightweight BIM-GIS, 28 IoT sensing nodes (water pressure, gas leakage, surface temp, <1 s delay) with 5-month pilot; addresses planning collision risks, construction rework, and delayed leakage detection; AI risk model predicted a valve aging risk 7 days in advance (verified on-site); 36.4% O&M cost reduction. One-way IoT→platform monitoring/decision support, no actuation and no self-improvement loop.', '04c-port'),
55: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'One-shot local Bayesian optimization + loss-weighted hyperparameter aggregation for federated learning (FL), integrated into a Digital Twin platform for device registration, orchestration, and telemetry (Jeju National U, Cluster Computing 2026): clients optimise hyperparameters locally on small data subsets, the server aggregates a single global set for collaborative training; training-method agnostic; evaluated on MNIST/EEGEyeState/Weather plus a private worker-safety dataset; 6.44% average end-to-end improvement, faster convergence, lower MAE vs simple averaging, reduced response time on Raspberry Pi AIoT clients; on-device inference supports near-real-time safety alerts to supervisors and wearables. One-way telemetry->prediction->alerts; FL retraining loop implemented but no convergence criterion and no physical actuation.', 'Endnote'),
62: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital urban twin for crisis management via modular distributed co-simulation (Fraunhofer SIRIOS): engineering-model simulation modules for water, electricity, gas, telecom, built environment and agent-based emergency response exchange events over a CloudEvents/FROST (SensorThings) event-stream architecture; mapping interdependencies and cascading failures among critical infrastructures; proof-of-concept on urban flooding/heavy-rainfall scenario predicting system states and structural impacts for authorities and training. Scenario-driven co-simulation; no live sensor loop demonstrated, no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
67: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Interconnected digital twins of subway stations for decision support (VIT/FRC RAS): per-station DTs interconnected to interact during operational scenarios; cameras, microphones, sensors processed in fog computing; mobile app with intelligent assistant displays detected events and answers queries via voice; event detection for hazardous situations (fire/explosion); implementation improved personnel response time by 17.4% vs REPEAT platform. One-way monitoring to event detection to decision support for operators; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
71: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Safety risk perception method for high-rise construction based on DT (Chongqing Polytechnic, IJCIS 2026): improved grey relational analysis screens safety influence factors; local linear embedding reduces factor-data dimension; DT architecture establishes a bidirectional mapping between physical construction space and virtual information space, defining a construction risk index with coupling influence terms; multi-level early warning thresholds embeddable in the existing site monitoring platform; experiments (incl. immersive-VR scenario data with EEG/eye-tracking plus sensor data) give recall 96.57-99.06%, accuracy 96.76-97.89%, perception time 0.62-0.87 s. One-way monitoring->risk perception->early warning; no actuation and no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
87: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Computer-vision-based digital twin framework for proactive near-miss prediction (Harbin IT): integrates real-time worker trajectories, postures and interactions into a dynamic 3D construction-site model; non-autoregressive transformer predicts future movement sequences (human motion model trained on Human3.6M dataset, inverse kinematics for joint angles) + collision detection identifies potential near-misses with early warnings; field-validated in three high-risk zones (forklift paths, floor openings, material lifting). One-way perception to prediction to early warning for safety managers; no actuation and no self-improvement loop (model is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
88: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin for advanced geological conditions in rock tunnel construction (Tongji U): multi-source geological data (water content, lithology, integrity) → multi-dimensional virtual models (geometric, attribute, behavior); fuzzy cloud probability model quantifies uncertainty for intelligent rock classification (92.95% accuracy); iS3 platform implements closed-loop data-model-decision; validated on five rock tunnel projects. Closed-loop data→model→decision→feedback → Tier 3; no learning loop (fuzzy cloud is probabilistic, not learning).', '04c-port'),
99: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Automated procedural modeling for tunnel inspection and digital twin development (USP): parametric modeling + field data → automated procedural modeling framework for tunnel inspection DT; PCD from Faro Focus 3D X330 laser scanner; Mesh Decimation Quality (MDQ) index evaluates mesh quality during decimation; procedural inspection grid identifies defects and classifies areas; Coastal Tunnel (Brazil) case study. Static DT for inspection — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
101: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Topology-guided Fourier Neural Operator (TG-FNO) with decoupled geometric parameterization for dam leakage detection (Chongqing Jiaotong U/HKUST): FNO replaces numerical solver for forward potential-field simulation (345x speedup, mean rel error 3.18%); decoupled geometric parameterization separates deterministic defect from stochastic background; Navigator network extracts coarse topological priors to initialize parallel multi-hypothesis workflow; 99.7% avg inversion success rate, 89.3% high-fidelity reconstruction, 72x overall acceleration vs FEM; robust to 20% noise and 50% data loss, detects unseen low-contrast early leakages, OOD generalization without retraining. One-way ERT->inversion->leakage localization for safety monitoring; implemented operator-learning surrogate (offline-trained), no actuation.', '04c-port'),
102: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'GUIDE2FR emergency-monitoring DT of a firefighter training tower (Alcorcón): Wi-Fi/LoRa beacon network (temp, humidity, CO2, TVOC) + RTSP video synchronised in a Grafana plugin; offline-trained ML forecasting pipeline (SVR/RF/Huber/GPR, forward-chaining CV, tested on 4 beacons at Fire Station 9) visualised in the DT; one-way data flow to human decision-makers, no actuation and no online learning loop.', '04c-port'),
107: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'DT x Transformer closed-loop intelligent construction system for high-rise self-climbing platform (HUST/UNSW): video/sensor/BIM/text aligned at component level via Component-ID+Timestamp; multimodal Transformer for operation-state recognition and short-horizon risk prediction; policy module encodes safety/resource/spatial precedence constraints to generate feasible task sequences delivered to crews via AR with acknowledgments to close the loop; validated on high-rise SCP project (extends risk-warning lead time, reduces violation rates, shortens decision latency). Bidirectional closed-loop (DT->reasoning->AR execution) -> Tier 3; no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
108: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Agentic AI-enhanced DT framework for smart-city civil infrastructure (Islamic U Madinah, PLOS ONE 2026): DT continuously updates asset/network models of bridges, roads and water infrastructure from multi-stream telemetry with state estimation, predictive maintenance and what-if simulation; LangChain/LangGraph Perception-Conceptualization-Action multi-agent workflow performs cross-domain reasoning and coordinated mitigation planning through controlled API calls; permissioned blockchain cryptographically binds observations, approvals and executed interventions; evaluated with 18,000 incident simulations (5 architectures x 3 complexity levels x 30 runs): mean detection latency 3,197 s vs 39,374 s, mitigation success 66.2% vs 45.5%, blockchain-anchored justifications 71.8%, operator workload -91.7%. Synthetic evaluation only (authors state no real-world operational validation); agentic recommendations with human operators; no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
111: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Reverse digital twin mapping of building envelope anomalies based on UAV infrared point clouds (Huaqiao U): PCRNet fuses infrared + point cloud data; CNN-based anomaly detection for regular/irregular geometric envelope structures; compares extracted temperature info with labeled abnormal dataset; 299 experimental data points, 92% accuracy, 96.3% precision, 94% recall, 95.1% F1-score, 5.21s detection speed. Static DT mapping — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
129: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital twin-driven system for road maintenance (TECNALIA): UAV + AMR integration for automated inspection and measurement of road assets; data fusion and real-time synchronisation between field agents and centralised DT; retro-reflectivity monitoring of signage, obstacle/vegetation detection; supports data-driven maintenance planning; case study on Italian highway network. One-way monitoring→DT→maintenance planning; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
142: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Conceptual paper (JCHMSD): socio-technical framework of multi-level interacting digital twins integrating social dynamics (values, senses, attitudes) with building and environmental data for heritage building management, adopting a Whole-Building and system-dynamics approach. No digital twin is built, implemented or empirically tested - the authors explicitly note the lack of empirical analysis and propose pilot testing as future work. P=No, R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', 'Endnote'),
143: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based framework for multi-objective optimization of shield tunneling parameters (Shenzhen U/HUST): layered architecture (data acquisition, preprocessing, modeling, optimization); SHAP identifies key parameters; ABC-NSGA-III hybrid optimization algorithm; optimized parameters iteratively fed back into DT to guide parameter adjustment; validated on Shanghai Airport Link Line project; 32.02% overall optimization rate, shield attitude deviation reduced 2.21-17.13%. Bidirectional — optimization→feedback→guidance → Tier 3; no learning loop (optimization is algorithmic, not learning).', '04c-port'),
145: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Reinforcement Learning (RL)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'DT-enabled synchronous jacking control of an aerial building machine (ABM) using a scale model (HUST): scale experimental platform; deep neural network (DNN-PID) for dynamic error compensation; reinforcement learning tunes control parameters; transfer learning migrates DNN-PID controller to scale model; DT system for visual presentation of jacking data and equipment states during synchronous control; jacking tests show 0.407 mm synchronization error (max <0.46 mm across 10 conditions), 29% max error reduction with fewer iterations; DNN-PID reduces MSE by 5.87 mm vs traditional PID. Bidirectional closed-loop (monitoring->control) -> Tier 3; implemented RL tuning + transfer learning (implemented learning mechanism, no convergence proof).', '04c-port'),
146: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Slope digital twin driven by an optimised surrogate model (stacking ensemble learning) for landslide safety monitoring: displacement prediction with multidimensional error analysis + adaptive parameter adjustment + model updating/retraining as a dynamic optimisation mechanism that "dynamically self-corrects against the Sim-to-Real gap"; error reduced 20% to 5% (validated with indoor loading + DIC experiments); Donglingxin landslide DT dynamically displays 2010-2022 deformation (acceleration-stabilisation, rate 12.5 to 15.5 to 11.8 mm/y). One-way monitoring to prediction/visualisation; implemented retraining loop but no convergence criterion/metric - AA=Implemented, not Convergence-characterised.', '04c-port'),
147: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Quality (DfQ)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Sky-space-ground integrated remote sensing monitoring DT framework for multi-source Data-BIM integration in residential quality monitoring (Beijing U Civil Eng & Arch, J Building Eng 2025): RBIM (residential building information model) aggregates full-lifecycle project data; SSIoT (surveying sensors + IoT) links physical things to cyberspace; multi-sensor monitoring (monitoring LiDAR, automated monitoring robots, GNSS, drones) with BIM collaborative multi-source data fusion; cloud platform unifies data processing/storage avoiding information islands; experiments: 8-phase LiDAR monitoring of a frame building tracking target-sphere centre displacement to assess building deformation trends, accuracy verification of self-developed LSIIS centre-extraction algorithm vs PCL/ICP/WTLS (Faro + Livox LiDAR), building settlement monitoring analysis with BIM-sensor linkage. One-way monitoring to DT platform for O&M quality management; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
149: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based multi-objective parameter identification for a cable-stayed bridge (SWJTU, Structures 2026): multi-objective optimization matches measured frequencies, mode shapes and deflections; adaptive reference-point relocation for irregular Pareto fronts, sensitivity-informed variation operators, hybrid quasi-Newton local search; case study on a 580-m cable-stayed bridge: up to 52% reduction in parameter-identification error and 25-35% runtime reduction vs NSGA-II/NSGA-III, errors consistently below 3% in robustness analysis; supports bridge condition assessment and maintenance optimization. One-way measured responses->model updating->condition assessment; no actuation and no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
154: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-enabled simulation system for NATM tunnel construction process considering multi-source uncertainty (Tongji U): five-dimensional DT concept with four-layer architecture (perception, transmission, modelling, alternation); integrated discrete event simulation (DES) model as core; Markov random field (MRF) for stochastic geological modelling; AHP-DEMATEL tunnel vulnerability evaluation + delay probability density functions for construction uncertainties; validated on a real-world tunnel project for schedule estimation, site communication, safe/efficient completion. One-way monitoring->simulation->schedule/safety decision; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
163: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Real-time maintenance monitoring system using BIM and digital twin integration (Sungkyunkwan U): LOD 400 BIM model of solar-powered noise barrier tunnel + IoT sensors (vibration, tilt, light, air quality, water detection) synchronized via Autodesk Forge API + WebSockets; web-based dashboard for visualization; anomaly detection via two-tiered approach (device alerts + post-processed trend analysis); validated on Wansan Tunnel in South Korea. One-way monitoring→visualization→maintenance decisions; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
169: ('No', 'No', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Systematic literature review of embedded concrete sensors (fiber optic, piezoelectric, capacitive, resistive) for SHM and service-life estimation, examining 71 Scopus/ScienceDirect articles (2022-2025); discusses integration with AI/IoT/BIM/ANSYS and digital twins only as reported in the reviewed literature. No digital twin is built, evaluated, or methodologically developed here; DfS/DfQ is about generic structural durability. P=No, R=No → Stage-2 exclude.', '04c-port'),
172: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Bayesian / probabilistic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Partially validated probabilistic framework for urban seismic damage prediction with scenario ensembles and DTs (IEEE Access 2026): four layers - data fusion, digital twin modelling, scenario ensemble simulation, probabilistic assessment; PI-GAN generates ground motions (<=5% PGA error, <=10% response-spectrum error); probabilistic damage-cloud module reaches 77.7% classification accuracy (79.5% recall, 87.3% precision, 83.2% F1) and 89.3% structure-damage matching, validated on the 2021 Yangbi Ms6.4 earthquake (single event, single region); cascading-failure and social-behaviour modules are conceptual only; M>=7.0 extreme scenarios and full-chain validation explicitly future work. Scenario/simulation DT - no live data loop, no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
180: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Physics-informed neural network edge-cloud collaborative DT for predictive maintenance of ageing railway signalling equipment (Shaanxi College, IJICT 2026): adaptive pigeon-inspired optimised PINN (API-PINN) integrates electromechanical degradation physics with operational data to forecast faults and estimate RUL; edge nodes run low-latency real-time anomaly detection, cloud performs model training; on real-world railway signalling datasets accuracy 98.77% and R2 0.968, robust under noisy and imbalanced data; enables proactive maintenance scheduling, cost and downtime reduction, safety improvement. One-way telemetry->fault/RUL prediction->maintenance decisions; offline-trained model, no actuation, no online learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
184: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'BIM-FEM-real-time monitoring framework for seismic assessment of Prince Moulay Abdellah Dam (Sapienza U): BIM digital replica interoperable with FEM simulations; real-time SHM sensor data captured during magnitude 6.8 earthquake (Sept 8, 2023); FEM analysis corroborated field measurements (abutments showed increased longitudinal displacement, central vault stable); BIM enables efficient monitoring data management. One-way monitoring→FEM validation→safety assessment; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
198: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', '120-yr heritage RC bridge; ambient vibration + laser displacement monitoring; FE-based DT validated against field data, used for what-if scenarios (overweight vehicles, scour loss); six-phase Incident Response Framework; model is updated/validated, not self-learning.', '04c-port'),
215: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 1, 0, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Semantic interoperability', 'Knowledge graph exploitation for construction safety planning (DTU): 4D BIM + automated safety analysis results → ontology + knowledge graph for cross-domain knowledge extraction; query building blocks transform natural language questions into actionable queries; case study shows cross-domain impact of decisions (e.g., crew assignment → safety). Static knowledge representation — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop (ontology/querying is static).', '04c-port'),
217: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Graph Neural Network (GNN)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'AI-enhanced DT framework for roadway serviceability under floods: GAT (graph attention network) couples flood simulation with INRIX traffic-speed data (5-min speed, 6-h flood intervals) to predict segment-level speed/accessibility 45 min ahead (test MSE 0.2602), capturing direct + indirect (rerouting) impacts; GIS/ArcGIS-based 3D DT visualization for emergency decision support. Validated on Hurricane Harvey (Houston, 2 zones); explicitly a "digital twin prototype" — live sensor ingestion "not yet automated", flood scenarios precomputed, no bidirectional feedback/control; offline-trained GNN, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
219: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT framework for predicting ground settlement and lining deformation of shield tunnels under adjacent excavation (NTU/Southeast U): hybrid surrogate model DF-STTN (Swin Transformer + TabTransformer) for full-field displacement prediction from spatial + non-spatial inputs; trained on high-fidelity FE data, then updated/validated on laboratory-scale tunnel excavation tests via a genetic-algorithm model-updating procedure that iteratively refines soil parameters using sparse test data (minimizing prediction error); outperforms convolution-based and single-fusion models; spatial info (3 measurement points) improves accuracy. One-way prediction with implemented GA-based model updating - no convergence criterion, no actuation.', '04c-port'),
230: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'BIM-enhanced DT architecture for construction pollution management in renovation (auditorium, Chulalongkorn Univ): five components (PE/VM/DD/Ss/CN), novel hybrid LOIN-LOD framework (LOD-G 200 as-is scan-to-BIM → LOD-G 350 as-designed) defining as-needed BIM information for DT; six IoT sensor clusters (PM2.5, CO2, noise, vibration) streamed via MQTT/Firebase into Node-RED rule-based engine with threshold alerts + React/Autodesk Forge dashboard; 1-s real-time monitoring. Bidirectional feedback/actuator control described but "implementation remains limited" — no automated actuation, no ML, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
238: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'LiBiDT causal LiDAR-BIM digital twin for streaming construction-site state (Sci Rep 2026): Spatio-Temporal Global Registration (LiDAR-IMU-GNSS priors), Multi-task Perception (PointNet++ semantic/instance/normal heads), Scan-to-BIM Association and State Updating (normal-guided point-to-plane refinement, bipartite matching with overlap/deviation/semantic evidence, EMA stabilisation); Decision and Risk Analytics layer outputs weighted completion, deviation summaries and three safety/compliance hazard flags; on CV4AEC 2024 Scan-to-BIM association F1 0.837, CD/RMSE 3.2/3.5 cm; held-out tile-stream case study shows state evolution and hazard-flag firing; strict temporal validation under active construction left to future work. One-way LiDAR stream->BIM state->management indicators; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
254: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'IFC-based framework for semantic integration of BIM and mobile crowd sensing in real-time evacuation routing (KNTU): IFC models transformed into dynamic decision graph with spaces/exits/sensors annotated by live crowd-sensed info; Wi-Fi-based indoor localization with two-stage crowdsensing; multi-criteria shortest-path routing via extended Dijkstra with dynamically updated weights (distance to hazards, travel time, exit availability, route safety index); AHP weight prioritization; implemented in four-story academic building. One-way monitoring→routing guidance; no actuation and no learning loop (Dijkstra is algorithmic, not learning).', '04c-port'),
258: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Systematic review + topic modeling of smart construction safety technologies (Kookmin U/Cyber Hankuk U): investigates DTs, IoT, big data for real-time monitoring and predictive risk management; develops conceptual framework for integrating smart technologies into safety systems; no DT built, evaluated, or methodologically developed - R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', '04c-port'),
260: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital-twin-driven bridge construction safety-monitoring platform (Zhanlin Yellow River cable-stayed bridge, incremental launching): dynamic multi-resolution DT (web-BIM model + Midas Civil FE model, 267 rod elements/19 stages); 120 embedded strain gauges + support-reaction/temperature/displacement sensors stream real-time to the twin; stress/deformation warning mechanism with 3 warning levels (e.g., stress deviation 11% → L1, 20-30% → L2, >30% → L3) triggers alerts to on-site personnel who adjust construction. One-way monitoring→analysis→human action; no automated actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
269: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'LSTM / RNN (recurrent networks)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Dual-loop collaborative smart-construction framework (Changsha UST, Discover Applied Sciences 2026): BIM + IoT + LSTM-Attention with an adaptive prediction-execution-feedback closed loop; 261-sensor deployment on the Taipei Bridge and Tunnel Joint Project with sub-second synchronisation; NSGA-II multi-objective optimisation over safety/cost/schedule/emissions. Statistically significant (p<0.001): 46.2% latency reduction, 41.4% fewer safety incidents, 18.5% direct-cost reduction, 11.1% CO2 reduction, 99.1% safety compliance. Closed-loop decision-making (prediction->execution->feedback) -> Tier 3; no self-improvement/learning loop (LSTM offline-trained).', 'Endnote'),
275: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'UAV-based framework for worker monitoring and management on large-scale construction sites (CUHK): pretrained YOLO-LCA model (detection accuracy improved 31.5%→96.4%) + multi-object tracking + 3D site reconstruction for precise global registration and situational awareness; cross-referencing UAV detections with GPS-enabled worker IDs for authorization verification; large-scale validation across multiple construction projects in Hong Kong; continuous UAV data collection enables iterative model retraining, improving detection robustness. One-way monitoring→authorization verification→decision support; implemented retraining loop but no convergence criterion.', '04c-port'),
278: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Safety Intelligent Navigation Platform (SINP) for tower crane climbing (HUST): systematic control framework integrating theoretical risk analysis (process analysis of key safety-critical points), GDTA-derived worker situation-awareness requirements, and a 4-layer digital twin virtual model (geometric/physical/behavioral/rule-based) with IoT-based real-time mapping/dataflow; edge intelligent control device (EICD) provides real-time safety navigation + alarms to workers, mobile monitoring for supervisors, cloud remote inspection; validated in indoor functional + outdoor practical experiments (task completion 515-676s→375-444s, errors 1.4-4.8→0, dialogues 11.8→0.8). One-way monitoring→navigation/alarms to humans; no automated actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
279: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Cross-project (multiple real projects)', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Automatic UAV inspection mission planning from a Geometric Digital Twin (GDT) and Voxelized Obstacle Information (VOI) (Guangxi U/DUT/Beihang, AutCon 2025): FOV-centroid parallel shifting generates structural-surface waypoints; environmental VOI from 3D point clouds adjusts waypoints for safety; GA + A* hybrid optimises collision-free flight paths; verified on an office building and a steel truss bridge with significantly improved efficiency. The twin is a static geometric reference for pre-planning; the UAV then executes the plan physically, no live twin link during flight, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
287: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Unclear', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Semantic interoperability', 'Systematic literature review (52 papers, Scopus+WoS, 2005–2023) on ontology/semantic-web/linked-data integration in BIM and digital-twin based construction management during the construction execution phase; identifies 8 use cases (incl. safety management, compliance checking, construction planning & production control); trend + theoretical analysis of how semantic-web tools (ifcOWL, BOT, SPARQL, SWRL) serve each use case; barriers: data privacy, scalability, ontology-mapping complexity. Review only — no DT built or tested; DfS/DfQ appear among reviewed use cases, not demonstrated; no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
292: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT framework for real-time building fire situational awareness (China Three Gorges U, Visual Computer 2025): AIoT sensor data processed by a Bert_C (BERT+CNN) model to analyse smoldering-to-flaming transition; 96.1% accuracy, 96.2% F1; numerical fire simulation generates training scenarios; 3D DT visualisation of fire scenes for firefighting and emergency rescue decision support. One-way sensor->prediction->warning/visualisation; no actuation and no learning loop (offline-trained).', 'Endnote'),
303: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Mentioned only', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Mobile gin pole (UHV construction): FEM kinetic analysis + TROA-ET surrogate (R2 0.9642) + NSGA-III safety-efficiency optimisation embedded in DT parallel-control architecture; bidirectional 4G/MQTT link (CANopen control commands) on real 110 kV project; safety risk -32.3%; surrogate is offline-trained, no online learning.', '04c-port'),
325: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 1, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Hybrid numerical method for evaluating seismic protection of buildings using dynamic FEM digital twins (NAS Ukraine et al., J Math Sci 2025): digital twins of the Pid Dubom residential complex (Lviv, Vrancea earthquake zone) driven by recorded soil-vibration accelerations from railway traffic and earthquake accelerograms; IoT sensor networks (cloud, online mode) feed the models; rubber isolators with nonlinear stiffness justified against Eurocode 8/DBN; overturning safety factors evaluated. One-way monitoring/records->FEM twin->protection design and safety assessment; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
331: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'AI-based ANN surrogate model for DTs in SHM of reinforced concrete bridges (Cervenka Consulting/CTU, RILEM SSCS 2025): ANN has two roles - calibrating the virtual twin to physical structure behavior, then deployment as fast-response surrogate providing safety information for ongoing SHM; physically informed deep learning trained from nonlinear FEM (ATENA) sensitivity analyses; demonstrated on Leonhardt shear-beam numerical example (100/400/1000-sample datasets) identifying material parameters (fc, ft, E, GF) from load-displacement diagrams. Numerical example only - no live data link to a real bridge, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
339: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'IoT+Digital Twin intelligent monitoring system for tunnel construction (Zhejiang Songyang): multi-source sensor network (environment, equipment, surrounding rock) + BIM dynamic modeling + risk intelligent analysis using improved D-S evidence theory (multi-source risk assessment with effectiveness factor and conflict weakening strategy); 100% monitoring coverage and 100% warning accuracy; captures palm face collapse and enclosing rock deformation time-sequence. One-way monitoring→risk assessment→early warning; no actuation and no learning loop (D-S evidence theory is rule-based fusion, not learning).', '04c-port'),
353: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Tunnel project in China; DT continuously integrates settlement/TBM/structural monitoring; KG rule-based reasoning infers hazards and mitigation; bidirectional DT-KG interaction visualised for decisions; prevention of further structural impact claimed in real emergency.', '04c-port'),
356: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Semantic interoperability', 'Cognitive Digital Twin modelling method for urban road emergency scenarios (Southeast U, JCCEE 2025): element-level and scenario-level twin models defined in geometry/attribute/behaviour dimensions with resilience theory; SysML + ontology modelling and a SysML2Ontology transformation tool build the Emergency Scenario Cognitive Digital Twin (ESCDT); case study constructs an ESCDT for a collision accident on the North-South Elevated Road (Shanghai) and uses it for scenario deduction in emergency management. Static scenario models for deduction; no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
363: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin-driven intelligent safety control for large-span steel mesh frame structures (Beijing U Tech): DT model built from actual engineering data + FE analysis; random forest algorithm analyzes influencing factors of overall jacking construction process (jacking height difference and jacking speed most influential); real-time monitoring + fault diagnosis; validated on airport reconstruction project. One-way monitoring→analysis→safety control; no actuation and no learning loop (random forest is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
379: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'MBSE-based design of a DT system for rotation-construction monitoring of a 90m+90m single-tower cable-stayed bridge (SWJTU): V-model architecture via RFLP (requirements-functional-logical-physical) process; SysML models for requirements/functions/behavior/integration; DT intended to predict risks and optimize rotation construction plans before implementation; MBSE improves design efficiency and early flaw detection. Design-phase work only - DT not yet implemented/deployed, model validation is future work; no live data link, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
381: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Simultaneous digital twin framework for building facade inspection (Tsinghua U): wall-climbing robot (negative pressure adhesion) with RGB camera + penetrating sensors; real-time vision-based defect segmentation (mAP 0.775) and metric quantification (length error 1.140 cm, center error 0.826 cm); cloud-based DT platform for quantitative defect visualization, spatiotemporal traceability, and data-driven project management; on-site inspection cycle latency 2.8-4.8s; validated on real building projects. One-way monitoring→DT→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
386: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Renovation Digital Twin (RDT) platform (Northumbria U, RINNO Project): pilot implementation on French demonstration site; real-time data + dashboards monitoring 13 KPIs across 5 domains (cost, schedule, quality, safety, environment); TAM evaluation (102 professionals, Attitude Toward Use RII 0.894); 73% emissions reduction achieved but economic viability challenges. One-way monitoring→dashboard→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
390: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT framework for damage detection and localisation of self-sensed CIPP-rehabilitated underground pipelines (Purdue/NDSU, Engineering Structures 2026): distributed fibre-optic sensors give high-resolution continuous strain; FEM + deep-learning strain-field correlation extend strain monitoring to structural deformation assessment; eccentric-compression experiments on bare and CIPP-lined steel substrates; DT enables real-time structural visualisation, early plastic-region identification and crack-severity quantification for predictive maintenance and pipeline safety. Lab experiments + numerical validation (no live pipeline deployment yet); one-way sensing->assessment; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
391: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Human-in-the-loop digital twin (HITL-DT) framework for smart civil infrastructure O&M (Beijing U Tech): fuses human cognition (perception, team situation awareness), AI, and engineering knowledge for risk sensing/diagnosis (spatiotemporal changes) and risk prediction/control; formalizes structural mechanics knowledge, embeds engineering code rules, expandable case knowledge base; multi-source spatiotemporal sensing (human inspection + machine vision). Human-in-the-loop bidirectional with human oversight → Tier 3; no learning loop (knowledge is rule-based, not learning).', '04c-port'),
399: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital twin-driven stability optimization framework for large underground caverns (Hanyang U): five-dimensional DT framework (physical objects, virtual objects, service systems, DT data, interconnections) with six modules (structure, geology, material, behavior, performance, environment); IFC standards for interoperability; seven-step methodology (geological assessment, virtual modeling, BIM-based design, construction, real-time monitoring, optimization); case study demonstrates improved deformation monitoring and rock support efficiency. One-way monitoring→optimization→stability management; no actuation and no learning loop (optimization is rule-based, not learning).', '04c-port'),
400: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Automated digitalization of engineered slopes for interactive digital twin visualization (HKUST): city-scale LiDAR point clouds → DrainNet (CNN, 81.26% Dice) for drainage channel delineation → automated parametric BIM modeling (Grasshopper, 9x faster than Dynamo) → web-based digital twin platform for interactive visualization and asset management. Static BIM models for visualization — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
405: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Edge-cloud collaborative digital twin for vibration anomaly detection and localization in high-rise buildings (Shenzhen U): wireless time-synchronized smart sensor (WTSS) with edge computing for anomaly detection; cloud server runs structural dynamics DT model for vibration source localization; BIM-based management platform for visualization; validated on 17-story high-rise teaching building with harmonic excitation tests. One-way monitoring→detection→localization; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
409: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'DT-enabled safety monitoring system for seamless worker-robot collaboration (Tsinghua U): depth camera + LiDAR perceive workers/robots/materials → geometric-solid virtual representations in a digital twin; computes separation distance (SD) and dynamic protective separation distance (PSD, per ISO 15066/13855); when SD exceeds PSD the system "accesses the physical actuators of robots to stop it" — explicit virtual→physical control (emergency stop). Experiments: 9.8 FPS, 0.177 s reaction latency, 0.09 m perception error, static+dynamic scenarios. No ML used and no learning loop (predictive motion methods are future work).', '04c-port'),
413: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin-driven pose estimation and trajectory prediction for modular integrated construction (MiC) on-site stacking (PolyU): UWB sensors + IMUs capture real-time dynamic activities of smart stacking objects; DT of stacking operations interacts with physical counterparts in real time for seamless mapping/visualization; PosTraFormer network (spatio-temporal feature fusion of trajectory point relations) for 6-D module pose estimation and trajectory prediction to provide stacking guidance; comparative experiments + case studies show higher trajectory prediction performance. One-way monitoring/prediction→guidance for crane operators; no actuation and no learning loop (PosTraFormer is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
416: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Single (one data type)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Geometric digital twin from airborne LiDAR for safety analysis of large-span spatial structures (HIT Shenzhen, J Build Eng 2025): one-dimensional geometric models extracted from point clouds capture real initial geometric imperfections of the Shenzhen Gymnasium retractable roof; FE models built from LiDAR measurements represent real structural performance better than the consistent-imperfection-mode method for stability/safety assessment. One-off measurement -> geometric twin -> FE safety analysis; no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
417: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Graph Neural Network (GNN)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Knowledge-data driven digital twin platform for tunnel face stability (TFS) prediction and control in large-diameter slurry shield construction (HUST): bidirectional synchronization between physical entity and virtual model; BO-GCN-BiLSTM + SHAP for TFS prediction (avg R2 0.935, RMSE 0.162 across 6 geological types); expert knowledge integration; control of TFS by maintaining slurry pressure within optimal range; validated on Wuhan Metro Line 12. Bidirectional — prediction→control → Tier 3; implemented BO-GCN-BiLSTM, no convergence criterion.', '04c-port'),
448: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Methodological framework for integrating SHM with numerical DT models for seismic assessment of heritage buildings (Basilica Maria Auxiliadora, Lima): numerical models in 3DEC and SAP2000 (modal + time-history of 34 seismic ground-motion records) identify susceptible zones and recommended sensor locations; sensor deployment and validation against experimental models are explicitly future work - no DT implemented, no live data link, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
460: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Both', 'None', 'LSTM / RNN (recurrent networks)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Five-dimensional DT framework for architectural heritage preventive conservation (BUCEA, J Build Eng 2025): physical entity, digital twin, twin data, service and connection dimensions; HBIM reconstruction plus structural linkage rule model and mechanics-based displacement trend model (LSTM) give real-time situational awareness and hyper-real-time extrapolation; prototype at the Yingxian Wooden Pagoda predicts spatio-temporal structural changes, supports disaster risk reduction and conservation decisions. One-way monitoring/prediction->conservation decision support; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
465: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'LSTM / RNN (recurrent networks)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'AIoT-powered building digital twin for smart firefighting and super real-time fire forecast (PolyU): AIoT-integrated DT maps building fires to digital fire scene; ADLSTM-Fire model transforms discrete sensor-array data into high-dimensional spatiotemporal temperature fields; forecasts fire development and hazardous regions 60s in advance; validated via full-scale building fire experiment; 93% reconstruction accuracy, 92% forecast accuracy. One-way monitoring→forecast→firefighting support; no actuation and no learning loop (offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
468: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Computer-vision-based digital twin framework for proactive near-miss prediction (Harbin IT): integrates real-time worker trajectories, postures and interactions into a dynamic 3D construction-site model; non-autoregressive transformer predicts future movement sequences (human motion model trained on Human3.6M dataset, inverse kinematics for joint angles) + collision detection identifies potential near-misses with early warnings; field-validated in three high-risk zones (forklift paths, floor openings, material lifting). One-way perception→prediction→early warning for safety managers; no actuation and no self-improvement loop (model is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
488: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 1, 0, 0, 'Both', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'PINN + BIM framework for prediction and optimisation of prefabricated-bridge structural performance (Anhui Vocational Colleges/ZSTU, Discover AI 2025): BIM provides geometry, material and construction-process data to build a digital twin; PINN embeds stress/strain/equilibrium physics into the network; optimisation algorithms refine design against safety, cost and environmental criteria; experiments show superior accuracy and generalisation vs traditional methods. Design-time simulation twin; no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
490: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'FL-based Safety Monitoring Digital Twin (SMDT) framework for multi-worker safety prediction (Jeju National U): DT platform + central FL server; edge devices (Raspberry Pi) represent workers and IoT nodes; real-world construction safety data (worker status, weather, structural parameters); dynamic node selection mechanism (normal distribution) optimizes global model convergence in FL; DT supports device registration, model creation, real-time control, visualization of FL training, and safety prediction. One-way monitoring→FL aggregation→safety prediction; implemented FL training loop but no convergence criterion.', '04c-port'),
493: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Transformer / Large Language Model (LLM)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Cross-project (multiple real projects)', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin system for a regional bridges group (Southeast U / Tongji): physical space collects vehicle info + structural response from bridges; digital space builds numerical models per bridge with traffic load as the linking variable; Transformer neural network predicts bridge responses (vehicle-load-based, within/cross-bridge, measured-data fusion) to enable safety warning across the regional network; validated on three concrete bridges in Jiangsu (vehicle driven over bridges; compared vs LSTM/BiLSTM/BiGRU; metrics Ta/RMAE/R²). One-way monitoring/prediction→safety warning & O&M decisions; no actuation and no self-improvement loop (offline-trained Transformer).', '04c-port'),
501: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Adaptable digital twin methodology for existing bridge management (HEIG-VD): integrates BIM + IFC (open interoperable formats) + ontology + FE models; laser-scanned 3D model converted to DT via IFC; enables structural analysis and what-if scenario simulations for maintenance decision-making; differential evolution algorithm for optimized FE model; case study demonstrates feasibility; cradle-to-cradle approach for end-of-life. One-way monitoring/analysis→maintenance decisions; no actuation and no learning loop (updates are manual inspection-based).', '04c-port'),
504: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Multisensory + BIM-integrated digital twin for urban excavation safety (Tianjin U, Shandong case): physical excavator equipped with multi-sensors, 3D pose estimated via kinematic model + social spider algorithm (SSA) (bucket-tip error 24.61 mm, translation accuracy +4.0 cm); BIM of buried utilities + 3D excavator model form a dynamic virtual model mirroring the excavation; physical-virtual coupled DT enables real-time safety control - dynamic collision-risk assessment with 3D visual guidance and safety warning (pipe model turns red when bucket enters risk area, operator stops) to avoid pipe-collision accidents; system prototype field-tested in two case studies, 0.05 s sampling. One-way monitoring to guidance/warning to the human operator; no automated actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
510: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Computer Vision / CNN / object-detection', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Earthwork digital twin for teleoperation of an automated bulldozer in mine edge dumping (Hulunbuir open-pit): three-stage DT — anterior-time (UAV tilt-photography 3D model, 0.6 cm avg error; improved BoundED point-cloud edge detection of retaining wall, precision 0.923/F1 0.877; blade-trajectory generation), real-time (5G teleoperation platform displaying video, radar obstacle detection, RTK/IMU attitude, force feedback, eye-tracking), posterior-time (big-data storage/analysis; +2 h/day effective work). DT provides real-time perception/visualisation for human teleoperation (control via operator, not automated by twin); no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
513: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Unclear', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 2, 'Design for Safety', 'Scoping literature review + Research-through-Design proposal of a conceptual framework integrating BIM-based digital twinning, Safety Management processes, and a Decision Support System (DSS) for OHS decision-making in building construction; outlines data/information streams, KPIs, real-time interfaces and worker engagement, and notes ML as a future requirement for real-time optimisation of assessment. Purely conceptual — no DT built, no experiment, no test; predictive/self-improving features only proposed as future work.', '04c-port'),
525: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Three Gorges Dam intelligent monitoring platform (Changjiang Spatial Info + CTG, Advances in Civil Engineering 2025): GIS+BIM digital base builds a DT geometric model of the hub; BIM+FE online rapid structural calculation and early warning; machine-learning analysis models mine monitoring data for intelligent prediction of potential safety hazards; IoT + Micro-INS digitises inspection workflows; workflow engine provides full-process digital collaboration. Real deployment at Three Gorges Dam; one-way monitoring->calculation/prediction->safety decision support; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
537: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Integrated intelligent approach for monitoring and management of deep foundation pit in a subway station (Shenzhen Metro Line 12 Waterlands Resort East Station): on-site geological investigation + 3D transparent geology on BIM platform; multi-source sensing (MEMS, BOFDA distributed optical fiber, laser radar, UAV, machine vision) for pit axial force/displacement/strain/temperature; BIM-based intelligent monitoring platform (proprietary cast modeling cloud platform); four ML neural networks predict key pit parameters - GA-BP achieved smallest error on this project; DT app terminal with 3D visualization, full-lifecycle monitoring, predictive analysis + AR combining BIM 3D model with real tunnel scenario. One-way monitoring to prediction to risk management; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
538: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Sensor acquisition and allocation for real-time monitoring of articulated construction equipment in digital twins (U Michigan): orientation sensors on backhoe loader boom/stick/bucket → real-time 3D DT visualization + proximity monitoring with preset safety thresholds → audio-visual warnings for operators; proof-of-concept for excavator operators preventing underground utility strikes; validation experiments characterize spatio-temporal discrepancies. One-way monitoring→DT visualization→warnings; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
548: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'DT framework of human-machine hoisting (tower crane, HUST): 1/30 physical scale model (sensors at 20 Hz) as physical entity + synchronous virtual model (FEM, BIM, component IDA) + IoT data flow for real-time dynamic stability analysis; four unsafe hoisting behaviors (vertical/tilt/sudden braking/unloading) compared (scale model vs simulation vs real-model simulation); collapse-probability level function ranks tilt hoisting as most dangerous, foundation/mast most vulnerable for sensor deployment. Lab scale-model experiment; warning to operator via threshold but no actuation and no learning loop (monitoring system design is future work).', '04c-port'),
550: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Intelligent tensioning method for prestressed cables via DT + AI integration (Beijing U Tech): fusion mechanism of DTs and AI for intelligent tensioning; multi-dimensional/multi-scale modeling for visualization; AI control center with closed-loop control framework; sensing equipment + intelligent algorithms for high-fidelity twin model and safety performance evaluation; enables dynamic perception, real-time processing, intelligent diagnosis, and intelligent decision-making. Closed-loop control framework → Tier 3; no learning loop (AI is control/decision, not self-improving).', '04c-port'),
551: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'BIM-enabled digital twin framework for real-time structural health monitoring (NJIT): wireless IoT sensing (strain gauges, laser displacement) + digital signal processing (WT with sym4 kernel optimal) + structural analysis domain knowledge; sensor data interpolation in Revit for visualization of structural behaviors at different locations; DT updating frequency of 5 Hz; validated on prototyped structural frame under bending forces. One-way monitoring→visualization→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop (interpolation is static mapping).', '04c-port'),
559: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Data and knowledge-driven bridge digital twin modeling (DK-DTM) framework for smart O&M (Beijing U Tech): multi-source data collection + spatiotemporal modeling + expert knowledge reasoning; real-time data from spatial/temporal models; expert knowledge model for automated structural health assessment; supports monitoring, prediction, and decision-making for efficient maintenance. One-way monitoring→assessment→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop (expert knowledge is rule-based, not learning).', '04c-port'),
566: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Unclear', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 2, 'Design for Safety', 'Scoping literature review + Research-through-Design proposal of a conceptual framework integrating BIM-based digital twinning, Safety Management processes, and a Decision Support System (DSS) for OHS decision-making in building construction; outlines data/information streams, KPIs, real-time interfaces and worker engagement, and notes ML as a future requirement for real-time optimisation of assessment. Purely conceptual — no DT built, no experiment, no test; predictive/self-improving features only proposed as future work.', '04c-port'),
569: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Bayesian / probabilistic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT of the tunnel geological environment for high-temperature water-inrush simulation (SWJTU, TUST 2024): voxel structure integrates multi-field attributes (stress, seepage, temperature); Gaussian-Process geological modelling fuses multi-source geophysical prediction data (TSP, TEM, IP, GPR); GP-Differential-Evolution back-analysis calibrates environment parameters; validated on a 230-m-burial ultra-high-temperature inrush tunnel in China and corroborated by tunnel monitoring data, supporting dynamic optimisation design and safety prevention during construction. One-way data->twin->simulation/safety measures; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
571: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based safety risk coupling framework for prefabricated building hoisting (Beijing U Tech, Sensors 2021): integrates IoT + BIM with Apriori algorithm (association-rule mining among hoisting risk factors) + complex network analysis of risk-factor coupling relationships, built as a DT coupling model; real-time perception and virtual-real interaction of multi-source hoisting information, with BIM visual display to guide on-site hoisting; validated on a large-scale prefabricated project, identifying key control factors. One-way monitoring/analysis→visual guidance for managers; no actuation and no learning loop (early-warning uses mined rules, not self-updating).', '04c-port'),
573: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Intelligent control of building fire protection (BFP) system using DT + semantic web technologies (SJTU): BFP ontology fuses static BIM geometric info + dynamic IoT sensing data into DT data model; rule model activates process model (workflow engine) for intelligent control mechanisms; DT data model synced with physical space; fire accident simulation case study demonstrates rapid response and evacuation facilitation; semantic web enables information acquisition/extraction/verification/update. Bidirectional — rule model triggers process model → physical actuation → Tier 3; no ML learning loop (rule-based control).', '04c-port'),
579: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Building process optimization framework based on BIM-DT (whole lifecycle: survey/design, construction preparation, construction, O&M): integrates data management system + BIM modelling system + digital twin model with real-time feedback; in the empirical study the construction phase data management system is built and a BP neural network is used for construction fault diagnosis (avg 99% accuracy vs CNN 90.23%, SVM 89.19%, PSO 88.35%; 9 fault types incl. construction joints, grouting, pouring sequence). One-way monitoring→fault diagnosis/safety; framework is partly conceptual (stage integration with BIM-DT model not described in detail — acknowledged), no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
580: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Integrated bridge DT system (Cardiff U): combines WebGIS (Cesium), WebBIM (Xeokit), and graph algorithms (Neo4j) in a three-layer architecture with a common data environment (CDE); enables real-time monitoring, drone-enabled inspection, maintenance planning, traffic diversion, and logistics optimization; adaptive data structure with JSON-based bridge defect information modeling and triple-based roadmap graphs; SHM system flags structural issues and triggers alerts/traffic redirection; defects from drone inspection inform maintenance planning. One-way monitoring→analysis→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
590: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Bayesian / probabilistic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'Intelligent overall planning model of underground space based on digital twin (Qingdao U): analytic hierarchy process for relative weight vector + Bayesian network for safety accident risk assessment; five-dimensional DT model for visualization and disaster prevention monitoring; real-time monitoring and analysis of underground space data; conceptual model with no DT built or validated; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
591: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Mentioned only', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'Four-layer DT-based fire-safety framework (physical/virtual/application/user-interaction) with explicit feedback "integrated back with the physical building layer for automatic control"; validated only via FM-professional questionnaire, no technical test; AI learning cited from literature, not implemented.', '04c-port'),
595: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'Mentioned only', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Building Digital Twin Platform (BDTP) architecture to overcome digitalization barriers for automating construction site management (TECNALIA, DSR + PDCA + Living Labs): diagnoses on-site inefficiencies and barriers via questionnaires/interviews; proposes standardized BPMN workflows with the DT as a service-oriented actor, modelling five cross-cutting domains (progress monitoring, quality control, OHS, equipment control, production planning) with digital/human agents connected via APIs; property-graph data model and use cases. Conceptual framework only — implementation, KPIs and AI/ML are "in the long-term"/future ("could be seamlessly implemented"); no deployed data link, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
598: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Vision/review paper (IEEE TITS 2025): reviews DT concepts in the North American freight-railroad industry and presents the vision of implementation layers for a DT of the FAST (Facility for Accelerated Service Testing) loop plus current efforts toward that vision. No digital twin is actually built or evaluated in the paper; methodological detail is about the vision architecture only. P=No, R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', 'Endnote'),
599: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Graphics-based digital twin (GBDT) framework for UAV-aided post-earthquake inspection of high-rise buildings (Guangzhou U/UIUC): FE model + photorealistic computer graphics (CG) model; CG model automatically imports structural components from FE model + adds nonstructural components; GBDT used to evaluate UAV flight schemes for inspection; FE analysis determines earthquake-induced damage locations; three UAV inspection schemes implemented virtually to select best. Static DT for inspection planning — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
604: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Tunnel digital twin construction and virtual-real fusion application (China Academy of Transportation Sciences): BIM technology constructs static tunnel scene model; 3D registration/projection integrates multi-channel surveillance video into 3D virtual scene in real time; multi-source sensing data fused for traffic flow, accident rescue, facility management, emergency response; management model for tunnel operations. One-way monitoring→virtual-real fusion→management; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
608: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based impact response prediction of prestressed steel structures (Beijing U Tech): high-fidelity DT from 3D laser scanning + BIM + FE simulation; improved BP algorithm predicts structural impact response; perception/transmission/analysis/service layers; validated on prestressed steel structure experiment. One-way monitoring→prediction→safety assessment; no actuation and no learning loop (BP is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
621: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Cross-project (multiple real projects)', 3, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Construction digital twin demonstrators (health & safety + progress monitoring) using Unreal Gaming Engine + CesiumJS mapping on a highway project (Skanska/UCL): location data integrates diverse sources; no-code approach for DT development; two case studies demonstrate 4D data presentation; explicitly described as human-in-the-loop DT (two-way communication with manual decision making) — virtual model changes reflect real-world changes, and humans act back on the physical site via decisions. Predictive capabilities discussed but not implemented; no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
622: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin aided vulnerability assessment and risk-based maintenance planning of bridges (Birmingham, Sustainability 2021): case study of Zhongcheng Village Bridge (Zhejiang, China); DT applications for bridge model establishment, information collection/sharing, data processing and inspection/maintenance planning; integrates DT/BIM with a bridge risk inspection model as an information platform to mitigate risks from extreme weather over the life cycle. BIM/inspection-data platform without a live sensor loop; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
625: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Agent-based model (ABM)', 'Single (one data type)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Hybrid simulation digital twin model for construction worker unsafe-behavior intervention (Central South U): closed-loop structured model with control panel, proactive management panel, and reactive panel; simulates workers behavioral safety under different intervention strategies using dual-attitude theory and reinforcement theory; proactive management maintains behavioral safety longer than reactive management. Simulation model only - no live data link to a real site, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
630: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Perspective article reviewing structural monitoring/evaluation/diagnosis for urban lifeline infrastructures; proposes a conceptual paradigm of integrated structural state-effect DT modeling and predictive diagnosis of hidden risks, and countermeasures for three bottleneck issues (multi-source point monitoring + area detection data fusion). No DT is built or validated and no specific methodology is implemented - R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', '04c-port'),
632: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Computer Vision / CNN / object-detection', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'BIM-based digital twin framework for post-earthquake building evaluation from UAV surveys: BIM guides automatic selection of optimal images per damage-sensitive component; GrabCut+nearest-neighbour segmentation assigns image pixels to BIM components (IoU 0.80–0.90); 3D point-cloud change detection (pre/post) identifies damaged nonstructural walls (std-dev indicator, threshold 0.010, correct at moderate-severe levels); damage tied to BIM to link with fragility curves + structural analysis for global safety. Example 1 = real Turner Hall RC frame; Example 2 = synthetic graphics. Framework not fully validated end-to-end (future PBGM work); one-way inspection pipeline, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
641: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Stava bridge (E6, Norway) incident study (SAP/NPRA, SIE 2024): the bridge DT processing IoT sensor data alerted a rapidly developing structural defect, enabling online and offline diagnostics and virtual inspection; physics-based methods combined with machine learning for damage detection and diagnosis; positions SHM and DTs within risk- and condition-based maintenance; damage was detected in time to stop development though not to avoid closure. One-way monitoring->diagnostics->human maintenance decisions; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
654: ('No', 'Yes', 'Yes', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Survey + case study on guiderail data management for a transportation agency: investigates current practices and proposes a data architecture for information-rich analytical models using DTs, but no DT is actually built or evaluated - P=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', '04c-port'),
666: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Single (one data type)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Joint-detection PCD-based method for automatic construction of geometric digital twin (DS-gDT) in cable dome structures (Beijing U Civil Eng): enhanced target-recognition algorithm with novel shape-estimation model samples minimum point sets to identify structural components; joints determined by component spatial relationships for topological reconstruction of the gDT; validated on scaled cable dome PCD (component segmentation success ~51.5% higher than traditional methods; joint fitting accuracy >99%); enables joint-deviation assessment. Static geometric DT - no live data link, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
677: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Reinforcement Learning (RL)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Deep RL (Advantage Actor-Critic) integrated with a digital twin for railway maintenance efficiency (Birmingham, Sci Rep 2023): DT built from four years of real field data over 30 km; track geometry parameters, component defects and maintenance activities form states/actions; rewards from maintenance costs and occurring defects; trained policy reduces maintenance activities by 21% and occurring defects by 68%, improving safety and passenger comfort. Maintenance-policy recommendations to decision-makers (no automated track actuation); RL training loop implemented but no convergence criterion.', 'Endnote'),
678: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Single (one data type)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'VR-based UUT management training simulator (Korea ETRI): digital twin of an underground utility tunnel modeled once from high-precision LiDAR scans, integrated with a 4-DoF motor motion platform; visual (HMD) + kinematic (fall, micro-vibration) feedback with cybersickness-reduction acceleration control; scenario content (facility installation, inspection, device repair); evaluated with 17 participants for cybersickness vs existing VR. Static reconstructed training replica — no live data link from a real asset and no learning loop; worker-safety training motivation.', '04c-port'),
687: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital twin-enabled heat risk monitoring for construction workers (Texas A&M): geometric digital twin of construction site + real-time weather station data + computational simulations for spatio-temporal heat risk analysis; case study in Stephenville, Texas, shows superior fidelity vs black-globe thermometer; near-real-time heat risk maps enable targeted interventions. One-way monitoring→simulation→risk maps; no actuation and no learning loop (microclimate simulation is physics-based, not learning).', '04c-port'),
700: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Single (one data type)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'Functional-safety methods for train control systems (NIIAS/TUEV Rheinland, RT&A 2023): a digital twin is defined as a mathematical model + software implementation performing all operating functions of the initial object + verification results; two same-type DTs form a dual external safety circuit so a SIL1/SIL2 control system reaches at least SIL3 (virtual second channels use information redundancy instead of hardware redundancy); evaluated analytically for an axle-counter-based train control system. The twin acts back on the control system as a safety channel -> Tier 3 (analytical safety-case evaluation, no deployed test); no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
704: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Structural safety risk prediction for terminal building steel roof construction (Beijing U Tech): DT model + FE analysis → sensor installation (hydraulic jacks, temperature, stress); XGBoost prediction model for stress changes of key rods (98% accuracy); compared GA-BPNN, RF, XGBoost; validated on airport renovation project. One-way monitoring→prediction→risk management; no actuation and no learning loop (XGBoost is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
716: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 1, 0, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital twin approach for underpass clearance checking in highway widening projects (UCL/HUST): online map data (DSM, DEM, aerial photos) → digital twin of existing main road + underpass road → BIM model of widened road; clearance check and redesign at preliminary design stage; cost-effective without field surveys; implemented on a UK underpass road. One-way design-stage analysis→clearance check; no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
722: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Computer Vision / CNN / object-detection', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Digital-twin-enabled anti-collision system for HRI safety on construction sites (5D DT: PE/DD/VE/SS/CN): multi-sensor fusion (RGB-D image+depth, IMU motion) + multi-modal analysis (YOLOv5/Faster-RCNN detection, HRNet excavator key-points) drive a Unity 3D virtual entity; rule model divides 3D site into dangerous/warning/safe zones (TTC+SO, d_danger=600 mm, d_warn=1200 mm) triggering collision warnings to smart helmets/tri-colour lights in a perception-analysis-decision-execution closed loop. Lab case study with 1:24 scaled excavator: zone warning precision 96.4%/95.3%, recall 98.8%/97.4%, delay 0.13 s. Warnings executed to humans/devices but no automated machine control; no self-improvement (manual retraining via data management).', '04c-port'),
723: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Real-world building digital twin for fire safety and anomaly detection (17 months of data, two use cases): advanced sensors + dimensionally-accurate 3D model + thermal camera sensors with real-time data fusion; features early fire/anomaly detection, fire localization and intensity evaluation, real-time incident data sharing, and fire-propagation simulation; data analysis predicts potential future threats. One-way sensing→visualization/simulation for operators; no automated actuation (integrating access-control actuation suggested as future work) and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
731: ('No', 'No', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'RETRACTED ARTICLE: This paper (A dynamic digital twin-based health monitoring method for steel structures integrating multi-source sensing and intelligent algorithms, Int J Structural Integrity 2025) has been RETRACTED by the publisher. Per SLR best practice, retracted papers must be excluded from the review. P=Q=R=No. The Endnote full text is flagged RETRACTED in its header.', '04c-port'),
736: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'DT construction method for monitoring operation status of building machine jacking operation (BMJO) (Hubei U Tech): DT framework with layered architecture; Blender geometric node group creates parametric virtual model; ANN enables online prediction of structural performance; motion model realizes real-time state mapping; real BM project validates system (quantitative monitoring, evaluation, early warning, real-time prediction of operational posture; high accuracy, fast analysis). One-way monitoring->prediction->early warning; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
745: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Bayesian / probabilistic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based risk control framework for prefabricated building hoisting (Beijing U Tech): DEMATEL-ISM establishes hierarchical safety risk model considering correlation between risk factors; Bayesian network visualizes decision analysis process for risk control; real-time data interaction with DT model; key degree of indirect inducement variables calculated by probability; validated on a large prefabricated building project. One-way monitoring→analysis→decision support; no actuation and no learning loop (Bayesian network is offline-inferred).', '04c-port'),
753: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Unclear', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 2, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Framework extending BIM Level-of-Details (LoDs) for construction-site digital twins: defines four core DT components (physical environment, digital representation/BIM, IoT, data storage-integration-analytics, interaction/feedback) plus new LoD-Graphics and LoD-Information (100–500) for construction-site components (site space, roads, facility, equipment, material, people) and maps minimum LoDs per BIM use/stage. Validated only via 31 questionnaires + 10 international expert interviews (>77% agree DT improves construction safety); no DT implemented or tested; feedback/autonomy described as future direction, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
758: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 1, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Lightweight digital twin of a crane boom for real-time structural safety monitoring using a multi-fidelity surrogate (MFS) model: low-fidelity surrogate (mechanistic, large LF data) + high-fidelity surrogate (statistical, small HF data) fused with live sensor inputs (inclination, strain at 18 test points) rendered in a Web app; real-time posture mirroring and stress prediction; uncertainty from physical-space sensors quantified (140-run trajectory data). Validated on a lab crane boom; MFS-RBF improves accuracy over single-fidelity and cuts cost vs numerical DT. Offline-trained surrogate, one-way monitoring/prediction — no online learning loop.', '04c-port'),
766: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Comprehensive survey of digital twin applications in civil infrastructure (SHM, predictive maintenance, smart cities, disaster response) reviewing methodologies, case studies and challenges (cost, interoperability, cybersecurity). DTs are the subject but the paper is a narrative/descriptive review with no original methodology, no framework, and no implementation to classify - R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', '04c-port'),
767: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Other', 'COWINE community DT ecosystem for disaster-resilient communities built on Cities:Skylines simulation engine with integrated real-world data (Brevard County FL pilot: topography, infrastructure, traffic, transit, disaster stats, 120k simulated agents); five-dimensional DT framing; collaborative stakeholder/public use-case for tornado preparedness/response/recovery with resilience-property analysis (vulnerability, robustness, redundancy, resourcefulness). Explicitly NOT real-time: "manual data-integration process", "human-based (manual) intermittent data flow", no automated calibration (future mods); no ML and no learning loop — descriptive, simulation-based.', '04c-port'),
772: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Intelligent prediction of prestressed steel structure construction safety based on BP neural network (South China U Tech): DT virtual model of construction process; BP neural network captures relationship between design parameters and mechanical parameters; working conditions set in twin model to obtain mechanical parameters, then safety performance evaluated; applied to string beam construction; predicted results verified against on-site measured data. One-way monitoring->BP prediction->safety assessment; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
774: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'DT evolution model for cable-structure demolition optimisation (BJUT, Structures 2024): virtual-real mapping of the demolition process via visual, simulation and data modelling; improved PSO-BPNN analyses mechanical properties across demolition steps to select the best construction scheme; a DT platform guides actual construction; verified on a cable-truss experimental model, accurately mapping the demolition process and improving visualisation and guidance. Experimental-model validation; one-way twin->guidance to construction crews; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
784: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Indoor safety management system (ISMS) based on digital twin, applied to a room in the Beijing 2022 Winter Olympics bobsleigh/sled stadium: IoT sensors collect real-time indoor operation data → BIM-based DTM maps real→virtual; SVM (support vector machine) trained to automatically classify danger types and assess danger levels from DTM data; functions include operation-status scene display, danger warning and positioning, danger classification/level assessment, and automatic danger-handling suggestions; synchronous virtual+real-world alarms. One-way monitoring/analysis→suggestions for staff; no actuation and no stated self-improvement loop (SVM is offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
785: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Vision-based risk assessment of jobsite windborne-debris impact on nearby dwellings: geometric digital twin of a gravel pile built from 45 UAV aerial images (dense point cloud + binarized DSM, volume 63 m³, EM ~4.6%) + semantic segmentation of glazing panels via CNNs (ResNet50 85.0% acc) from Google Street View + satellite terrain modeling; reliability of glazing systems computed with FEMA-HAZUS windborne-missile model (N_adjusted ~237 impacts at 62 m/s, 80 m). Static one-shot reconstruction/analysis — no live data link and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
791: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'LSTM / RNN (recurrent networks)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin model theory for tunnel construction safety assessment (Beijing U Tech): IoT + smart sensors collect project data; DT built combining BIM + Midas + LSTM ML algorithm; black-box/gray-box/white-box hierarchical data processing; vault (arch crown) settlement predicted with high accuracy and dynamic safety-state assessment during tunnel construction. One-way monitoring->prediction->assessment; no actuation, no learning loop (LSTM offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
793: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Quality (DfQ)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Cross-project (multiple real projects)', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', "DT-based monitoring pipeline for slated pitched roofs (University of Edinburgh / Historic Environment Scotland): (1) automated occlusion-free roof-panel orthophoto generation from SfM photogrammetry + the building DT/BIM model; (2) deep-learning semantic segmentation of orthophotos into slates/leadwork/other (PointRend+Focal Loss best, background corrected to 100%); validated on 3 real traditional buildings (Duff House, St Mary's Church, ...). Outputs are semantically linked to DT/digital logbook elements for future defect detection and epoch comparison; processing pipeline is static/offline — no live data link and no learning loop.", '04c-port'),
794: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', '2-year in-service railway bridge pilot; unsupervised clustering of normal vibration + FEM-calibrated synthetic damage + LightGBM classifier (ROC-AUC 0.9999); periodic retraining of the model on accumulated data = implemented learning loop, but no convergence criterion/metric.', '04c-port'),
796: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Multisource information fusion for real-time prediction and multiobjective optimization of large-diameter slurry shield attitude (HUST): BO-CatBoost prediction model (R2 > 0.9, RMSE < 1.2, MAE < 0.9 across 3 soils) + MOEAD multiobjective optimization; SHAP identifies propulsive thrust as most influential; DT framework for SA control; validated on Yangtze River large-diameter slurry shield project (Wuhan). One-way monitoring→prediction→optimization; no actuation and no learning loop (offline-trained).', '04c-port'),
800: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital twin-based investigation of a building collapse accident (Tsinghua U): virtual digital building models (BIM, FE model, physics-engine model) built from real-world info; real-world data mapped into virtual space to construct highly realistic multistage models before and after the collapse, synchronized; investigators integrate/update/check models to reveal collapse mechanism; validated on a real collapse accident (columns exceeded critical buckling stress from welding-induced local buckling/plastic deformation). One-way data->model->cause diagnosis; no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
811: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Informative digital twin (IDT) based fire emergency management system (Sehan U/KUT): cloud-edge-device layers; edge-layer IDT built with object-oriented design gathers/processes building state data; fire recognition via online DTW similarity measurement between real and simulated virtual sensor data; risk assessment with ARET/RRET/SM metrics per zone; case study shows 0.88s fire recognition processing time and 65s evacuation time reduction. One-way monitoring→fire recognition→risk assessment; no actuation and no learning loop (DTW is similarity matching, not learning).', '04c-port'),
812: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Intelligent safety-monitoring DT system for large underground space construction (Shanghai Baoye/BJUT, Buildings 2024): BIM builds the physical construction model; IoT collects multi-source heterogeneous monitoring data in real time; virtual-physical information exchange enables real-time security analysis whose results are fed back to the application service layer; verified on an example project, obtaining parameter-index mapping for the orthogonal arch and reasonable control measures. One-way monitoring->analysis->feedback to managers; no actuation, no learning loop.', 'Endnote'),
813: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Digital-twin based multi-information intelligent early warning and safety management platform for tunnel construction (CUGB/Beijing Jiaotong U): WSN base stations for instruction sending, warning, positioning, information transmission; multi-source sensors (safety, environmental, construction, auxiliary) integrated; four-level early warning and emergency response plan; validated on Dongtianshan Tunnel (deep buried, extreme weather, harmful gas); collapse accident successfully predicted. One-way monitoring→early warning→management; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
827: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Real-time mixed reality-based visual warning system for construction workforce safety (RMIT U): integrates BIM + CV + DL; VCS simulates construction activities, identifies hazards from BIM models + real-time camera info; wearable MR devices present hazard information to workers for proactive actions; three outdoor tests; 96.1% hazard identification accuracy, 424ms delay, 72m² effective area. One-way monitoring→hazard identification→warnings; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
843: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'Modelling study of prefabricated building construction process using digital twins + prefabricated BIM (Chongqing Jiaotong U): DT/prefab construction system with measuring sensors for real-time monitoring and prediction of component damage/deformation (production, transport, assembly); assembly BIM transferred to network cloud for BIM display; risk-indicator data analysed with factor analysis (Cronbach alpha 0.8-0.9, KMO, variance 65.02% cumulative) for potential safety hazards during construction. One-way monitoring/prediction→designer guidance; no actuation and no self-improvement loop (data collection is narrow — acknowledged limitation).', '04c-port'),
846: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DT-based construction safety-management model for large engineering structures (48 m-span steel roof): DT generates real-time structural state samples that train a PSO-optimised BP neural network for vibration displacement / stress prediction (vertical displacement PA 98.2%, cable stress PA 99.1%, EV 0.978); validated only on a numerical model under 5 simulated working conditions; monitoring-and-warning only, no actuation, offline-trained predictor, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
847: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'BIM-driven closed-loop digital twin framework for human-robot collaborative construction (TAMU/U Michigan): BIM drives robot functions; robot adaptively adjusts plans based on actual site conditions; human co-worker oversees and intervenes (change task sequence, workspace geometry, new motion plan); as-built information sent back to BIM forming closed-loop; drywall installation case study + Gazebo simulation + physical robotic arm experiments. Bidirectional closed-loop — BIM updated with as-built data → Tier 3; no learning loop (adaptation is rule-based, not learning).', '04c-port'),
850: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Design for Safety', 'DT+IoT multi-information monitoring system for arch-cover method subway station construction (Shikui Road Station, Dalian Metro Line 5): automatic sensor network (settlement, stress, etc.) → IFC extension + Revit BIM parametric sensor models → BIM database visualization with time-history curves and color-change early-warning; "Construction Control Based on Data Analysis" uses monitored data as control value for decisions, but the loop is human-in-the-loop (feedback to decision-makers), not automated actuation; no ML, no self-improvement.', '04c-port'),
856: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital twin system for a regional bridges group (Shanghai, Tongji U): physical space - WIM + multi-source machine vision traffic-load monitoring on target bridge + lightweight sensors on bridge group; digital space - mechanical analysis models per bridge linked by measured traffic loads for working-condition perception and safety warning across the regional network; preliminarily implemented in a Shanghai bridges group. One-way monitoring to analysis to warning for operators; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
858: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'Lifecycle / governance', 'Risk systematization approach for construction projects using Digital Twins for Construction Projects (DTCP) (UT Cluj-Napoca): reviews risks and proposes risk treatment procedure + custom risk matrix adapted to DTCP; aims to improve prediction capabilities for decision-makers; conceptual framework with no DT built or validated; no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
867: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Digital twin model for monitoring building structural health by combining BIM and real-scene 3D model (Nanjing Tech U): fuses BIM with real-scene 3D model via rigid-body transformation (3D spatial position registration) + semantic information mapping (JSON); reconstructs BIM into sub-BIMs; sensor data stored in database and integrated with fused model; Nanjing Museum Old Hall case study. One-way monitoring→fusion→visualization; no actuation and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
868: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Single (one data type)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Digital-twin-assisted fault diagnosis for construction-robot joints (RV reducer): gear-dynamics virtual-entity model generates faultless vibration (X-domain), CycleGAN maps virtual→physical domain using only ~400 measured samples (Y-domain), and CNN-ResNet classifies wear/crack/pitting/normal faults — accuracy raised from 32.5% (measured only) to 98.86% with 1200 simulated samples (best of GAN/transfer baselines). Validated on a lab RV-reducer test rig with acceleration/temperature sensors; DT is an offline data-augmentation/generative model for training, no live twin loop, no learning.', '04c-port'),
876: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Unclear', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 2, 'Other', 'Review + methodology proposal for "physical digital twins" of ancient corbelled stone masonry (Sardinian nuraghi, cultural heritage): combines historical analysis of original construction techniques (dry masonry, thrust-free pseudo-domes, block distribution) with proposed mechanical-modelling approaches (discrete-element / variational-inequality granular models, multiphysical weathering: water diffusion, salt crystallisation, thermal, chemical) to assess structural safety and predict preservation-state evolution. No DT is actually built or validated — approaches are "possible roads... under investigation for future structural studies"; no live data, no learning.', '04c-port'),
885: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Statistical / change-point', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Dam digital twin (Jiangya dam, 131 m gravity dam) for automated continuous safety evaluation: extended IFC data schema (IfcDSMSystem/IfcMonitoringItem/IfcSensorAssembly) integrates DSM monitoring information (deformation, seepage, stress, environment); HST statistical models set baselines; multi-rule cloud-reasoning model evaluates monitoring points, multi-dimensional cloud model + improved CRITIC (no-human weights) aggregate to five-grade dam safety status. Case: continuous evaluation Jan–Sep 2019 → "basically normal". One-way monitoring→automated evaluation→human decisions (preventive maintenance); statistical models are regression fits, no self-improvement loop.', '04c-port'),
886: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Intelligent risk prognosis and control of foundation pit excavation (FPE) based on DT (Beijing U Tech): physical space (RFID + sensors capture components, environment, personnel) + virtual space (high-fidelity physics-based model); data fusion from physical and virtual space; FE model (FLAC3D) updated with real-time parameters; geometric model updated via point data; risk prognosis and control measures established based on safety state; validated on Wuhan Metro Line. Bidirectional — virtual model updated from physical, control measures from virtual → Tier 3; no learning loop (model updating is manual).', '04c-port'),
894: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Enriching geometric digital twins of buildings with small objects (TUM/Cambridge): fuses laser scanning + photogrammetry; AI-based image segmentation (deep learning) detects small objects (electrical, fire-safety, plumbing); AI-based text detection/recognition extracts object IDs; semantic info mapped to 3D point cloud → enriched DT with geometric + semantic + text info; comprehensive case study. Static DT for facility management — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
895: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Early-warning of unsafe hoisting operations via DT + knowledge graph (HUST): DT framework mirrors real-time operational status of tower crane (lifting, luffing, rotation); knowledge graph identifies unsafe hoisting operations by leveraging real-time data from the DT; scaled-down tower crane replica in lab; warning rate >70%, false alarm rate <20%. One-way monitoring→KG analysis→early warning; no actuation and no learning loop (KG is rule-based).', '04c-port'),
901: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Digital Twin platform (no machine learning)', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Conceptual (no test)', 3, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Systematic review (146 articles) of bridge disaster management + proposed Real-time Bridge Disaster Management (RtBDM) framework: dynamic adaptation + digitalisation (BIM/DT integration for full-lifecycle data management and automated decision-making) + disaster cycle (pre-warning, real-time response, post-disaster recovery); addresses interoperability, delayed response, and coordination gaps. Framework only - no DT built or validated; no live data link and no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
904: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Finite Element Method / physics-based', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'BIM-to-Digital-Twin architecture', 'Dynamic geometric digital twin (gDT) for spatial cable-net structure construction (Shanghai Jiao Tong): multi-stage laser scanning extracts geometric info → parametric IFC/BIM (cables as straight segments, clamps as Revit families) + ABAQUS FEM (shape & force prediction); previous-stage FEM + construction progress + temperature data fill gaps between scan stages to build a continuous dynamic IFC model; stage modelling+computation <140 s, BIM-vs-point-cloud avg 15-20 mm, next-stage cable shape/force prediction deviations 1.3%/1.5%. One-way physical→virtual stage-by-stage update with prediction; no actuation and no learning loop (manual re-parameterisation).', '04c-port'),
914: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'DTCRAM: five-layer DT construction-risk assessment model (physical twin / data twin / twin model / data analysis / decision feedback) built via 3-round Delphi (9 experts, 15 risks incl. worker safety A1, equipment safety A2, construction quality A3) + case study (Thames Tidal Tunnel); real-time sensor data feeds simulation/risk prediction; claimed ~1% risk-probability reduction per project (A2 5%->3%, C1 3%->2%) but figures are estimates; feedback/optimisation loop described conceptually, not a demonstrated learning mechanism.', '04c-port'),
919: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 3 - Digital Twin (bidirectional, two-way)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Interactive and immersive process-level digital twin (I2PL-DT) in VR for collaborative human-robot construction work (Univ. of Michigan): human in VR does high-level task planning/supervision and trajectory guidance; KUKA mobile robotic arm (emulator) does sensing, motion planning (SBT/motion-plan generation, collision-free) and physical execution via ros_control + PID to real actuators; seamless bidirectional communication between human and robot with real-time robot status supervision; augmented telepresence prevents workers from exposure to on-site hazards (safety benefit); drywall installation case with imperfect framing, 20-subject human-in-the-loop study. Genuine virtual→physical robot control → Tier 3; no ML learning loop.', '04c-port'),
924: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Brillouin fibre-optic sensors + mobile augmented reality digital twin for underground pipelines (Dalian UT, AutCon 2022): distributed BFOS networks measure unpredictable deformations (longitudinal bending, axial thermal strain); a joint data-physics driven model estimates structural stress states more accurately than common calculation models; MAR-based human-asset interface enables intuitive, efficient and automated O&M; field experiments demonstrate quantitative safety assessment and prediction from the DT. One-way sensing->assessment/prediction; no actuation, no learning loop; in-line robotic systems left as future work.', 'Endnote'),
925: ('No', 'Yes', 'No', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Literature review + bibliometric analysis (Structures 2025): systematically reviews digital-twin-enhanced health monitoring and condition assessment of cable-supported bridges and proposes a novel three-layer DT framework with seven challenge areas and future trends. No DT is built, evaluated or methodologically developed in this paper (framework proposal only). P=No, R=No -> Stage-2 exclude.', 'Endnote'),
927: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Quality (DfQ)', 'None', 'Ontology / semantic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Semantic interoperability', 'Quality defect trigger identification in a construction digital twin (Southeast U): evolution-mechanism + ontology-based four-layer semantic model (quality standards / quality data / defect triggers / construction processes) implemented in GraphDB for semantic linkage of multisource heterogeneous data; an iterative deviation-computation engine (process logic + rule constraints) identifies potential quality defect triggers and visualises them in the DT; validated on a real prefabricated composite-slab installation case + comparative experiments + expert evaluation. One-way data integration→reasoning→identification/visualisation for proactive quality management; no actuation, no self-improvement loop.', '04c-port'),
937: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'None', 'Perception / Computer Vision', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Design for Safety', 'Vision-based digital twinning and threat assessment for construction site disaster preparedness (Texas A&M): deep learning encodes disaster risk context into construction site digital twin models to identify and analyze potential wind-borne debris characteristics and impacts; case studies on nine piles of construction materials; rapid 2D/3D semantic segmentation for vulnerability flagging. Static DT for risk assessment — no live data link, no actuation, no learning loop.', '04c-port'),
938: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 1 - Digital Model (static, no live data)', 0, 1, 0, 'Both', 'Mentioned only', 'Other / Mixed', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Simulation', 3, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'Computational digital twin with material characterisation for robotic adaptive 3D concrete printing (XJTLU, Struct Control Health Monit 2026): Grasshopper parametric workflow implements a compressive-strength predictive model with Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation (1000 samples), optimising process parameters to maximise parallel strength and guarantee grade M20 at the 5th percentile (design-for-safety); variance in parallel structural strength reduced by 25% with 90% confidence of M20, reducing anisotropy; a pretrained LLM acting as high-level orchestrator for closed-loop control via few-shot in-context learning is proposed/PoC-described but the closed loop is not demonstrated on the physical cell (no test-bed experimental data). Virtual-testing validation; no live physical link; learning mechanism mentioned only.', 'Endnote'),
942: ('Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Tier 2 - Digital Shadow (one-way physical to virtual)', 0, 0, 1, 'Design for Safety (DfS)', 'Implemented', 'Bayesian / probabilistic', 'Multi (two or more data types)', 'Single case study', 4, 'Predictive analytics / decision support', 'System digital twin (SDT) for life-cycle risk assessment of bridge networks: Bayesian network (BN) integrates multi-source data (NBI bridge inspections, FDOT traffic/AADT, USGS river gage) to update bridge failure risk (superstructure + scour) over time via automated Bayesian inference (indicator matrix for annual updates; network risk profile trends up as data update reduces uncertainty). Miami-Dade County case: 1,034 bridges, 6,478 nodes, 10,584 edges; 3 flexibility scenarios (new bridge, decommissioning, climate-change flood with CPT recalibration). Updating is implemented Bayesian inference — but authors state framework "has not yet been validated"; CPT refits are manual, no autonomous learning loop.', '04c-port'),
}

